{"name":"Hickory Tint","hex":"#bc916f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hickory","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various deciduous hardwood trees of the genera Carya and Annamocarya, one species of which, Carya illinoinensis, is the source of pecan nuts.","The wood of these trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hickory"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hickory","blocks":[{"text":"Hickory is a common name for trees composing the genus Carya, which includes 19 species accepted by Plants of the World Online."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Carya_Morton_29-U-10.jpg/330px-Carya_Morton_29-U-10.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hickory","wikidata":"Q142788"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Carya_cathayensis_nuts.jpg/500px-Carya_cathayensis_nuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig